build/
# The bare pattern above matches any directory literally named "build" at any depth (equivalent to
# **/build/) -- intended for the top-level CMake build output directory, but it also silently
# swallows these two real SOURCE directories of build-related shell/Python scripts (found the hard
# way: three new .py files added under arcology-os/scripts/build/ never showed up in `git status`
# at all). Re-included explicitly rather than anchoring the pattern to `/build/`, since several
# OTHER nested "build" directories in this tree (lazarus/build, arcoflow/build, games/build,
# lazarus-os/build, etc.) genuinely are build-output directories that should stay ignored.
!arcology-os/scripts/build/
!scripts/build/
!fissure/adapters/build/
build-*/
dist/
/var/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt

*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
*.exe

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Legacy root-level generated/runtime artifacts (new output belongs under dist/ or var/)
arcoalpha/
arcoalpha.zip
arco-file-log-example.txt
*.acpy
*.acdb
*.arcodb
*.arcodb.journal
